          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Cartesian fibrations are one of the types of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations+of+quasi-categories"} fibrations of quasi-categories
          %p
            A
            %em Cartesian fibration
            of quasi-categories – or more generally of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            incarnated as
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
          %p
            It is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+fibration"} inner fibration
            that lifts also all right
            %em outer
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
            inclusions whose last edge is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+morphism"} cartesian morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+morphisms"} cartesian morphisms
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+fibration"} inner fibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : C \to D
            may be thought of as a family of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} (infinity,1)-categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C_d)_{d \in D}
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial"} functorial
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            only in the sense of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            being a cartesian fibration ensures that the family is actually
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial"} functorial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : C \to D
            is a Cartesian fibration, then it is possible to interpret its value over any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : d_1 \to d_2
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{-1}(f) : p^{-1}(d_2) \to p^{-1}(d_1)
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{-1}(d_2)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{-1}(d_1)
            over its source and target
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
          %p
            This way a Cartesian fibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : C \to D
            determines and is determined by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^{op} \to (\infty,1)Cat
            into the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
          %p
            Cartesian fibrations over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            are the fibrant objects in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+marked+simplicial+over-sets"} model structure on marked simplicial over-sets
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %h2#definition Definition
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to Y
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              is a
              %strong Cartesian fibration
              (or
              = succeed ")" do
                %strong Grothendieck fibration
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  it is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+fibration"} inner fibration
              %li
                %p
                  for every edge
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi x
                        %mo →
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : x \to y
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                  and for every lift
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat {y}
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                  (that is:
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mover
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(\hat{y})=y
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+morphism"} Cartesian edge
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo :
                        %mover
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo →
                        %mover
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{f} : \hat{x} \to \hat{y}
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  lifting
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  (that is: such that
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mover
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(\hat f) = f
            %p
              The morphism is a
              %strong cocartesian fibration
              (or
              = succeed "," do
                %strong Cartesian opfibration
              = succeed ")" do
                %strong Grothendieck opfibration
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+quasi-category"} opposite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mi op
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{op} : X^{op} \to Y^{op}
              is a Cartesian fibration.
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, def. 2.4.2.1
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Given cartesian fibrations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to C
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q : Y \to C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Map
                      %mi C
                      %mi cart
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msub
                      %mi Map
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Map_C^{cart}(p,q) \subseteq Map_C(p,q)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Fun
                      %mi C
                      %mi cart
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msub
                      %mi Fun
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fun_C^{cart}(p,q) \subseteq Fun_C(p,q)
              be the full subsimplicial sets spanned by the functors that preserve cartesian morphisms. We call such functors
              = succeed "." do
                %strong cartesian functors
            %p Dually, we make the analogous definition of cocartesian functor.
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Map
                      %mi C
                      %mi cart
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Map_C^{cart}
              are the mapping spaces in the (cartesian) model structure on marked simplicial sets over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#general_properties General properties
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p We have:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                  is a Cartesian fibration.
              %li
                %p The composite of two Cartesian fibrations is again a Cartesian fibration.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              This is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 2.4.2.3
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Every Cartesian fibration is a fibration in the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Joyal"} Joyal
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              This is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 3.3.1.7
          %h3#BehaviourUnderPullback Behaviour under pullback
          %p
            Since a Cartesian fibration is in particular an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+fibration"} inner fibration
            and since inner fibrations are stable under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : E \to C
            a Cartesian fibration, the fiber
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_x
            over every point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in C_0
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  E_x &amp;\to&amp; E
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\{x\} &amp;\to&amp; C
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            The difference between inner fibrations and Cartesian fibrations is that only for Cartesian fibrations is it generally guaranteed that these fibers over the points are
            %em functorially
            related over the morphisms in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
          %p But moreover:
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The pullback of a Cartesian fibration in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              is again a Cartesian fibration.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              This is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 2.4.2.3
            %p
              We know from the discussion at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+fibration"} inner fibration
              that the pullback is an inner fibration. It remains to check if it has enough
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+morphism"} Cartesian morphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop 2.4.1.3
              we have that in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi q
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi p
                                  %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    E' &amp;\stackrel{q}{\to}&amp; E
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{p'}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    C' &amp;\stackrel{k}{\to}&amp; C
                    }
            %p
              a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in E'
              is
              = succeed "-Cartesian" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p'
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q(f)
              is
              = succeed "-Cartesian." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E'
              are pairs of morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi γ
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\gamma, \hat f) \in C'_1 \times E_1
              and since by assumption
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is a Cartesian fibration, there is for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma \in C'_1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in E'_0
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p'(y)
              is the target of the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
              a Cartesian lift
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat f \in E
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k(\gamma)
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q(y)
              is the target of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi γ
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\gamma, \hat f)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E'
              having
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              as target.
          %p We can test locally if a morphism is a Cartesian fibration:
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+fibration"} inner fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to Y
              is Cartesian precisely if for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \leq 2
              and for every
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma : \Delta[n] \to Y
              the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi σ
                      %mo *
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Y
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma^* p : X \times_Y \Delta[n] \to \Delta[n]
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi Y
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi σ
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X \times_Y \Delta[n] &amp;\to&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    \\Delta[n] &amp;\stackrel{\sigma}{\to}&amp; Y
                    }
            %p is a Cartesian fibration.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              This is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, cor. 2.4.2.10
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              of a weak equivalence in the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Joyal"} Joyal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
              along a Cartesian fibration is again a Joyal-weak equivalence
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              This is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop 3.3.1.3
          .un_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              Equivalences in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Joyal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
              are stable under pullback along Cartesian fibrations:
            %p if
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi S
                            %mi T
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X \times_S T &amp;\to &amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    T &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; S
                    }
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              square in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \to S
              a weak equivalence in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Joyal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to S
              a Cartesian fibration, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi S
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times_S T \to X
              is also a weak equivalence.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              This is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 3.3.1.3
          %p
            The following proposition asserts that the ordinary pullback (in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                            %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\to&amp; X'
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    S &amp;\to &amp; S'
                    }
            %p
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              of quasi-categories, where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X' \to S'
              is a Cartesian fibration. Then this is already a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              diagram with respect to the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
          .proof
            %h6#proof_7 Proof
            %p
              This is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop 3.3.1.4
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} T \to S'
              into a weak equivalence and a fibration in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Joyal
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mi S
                                %mo ′
                            %mi X
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                            %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\to&amp; T \times_{S'} X'&amp; \to&amp; X'
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    S &amp;\to &amp; T &amp;\to&amp; S'
                    }
            %p
              is the ordinary pullback over a fibrant replacement of the original diagram hence is a homotopy pullback. The claim follows thus if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo ′
                    %mi X
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to T \times_{S'} X'
              is a weak equivalence, which it is by one of the above lemmas.
          %h3#straightening_and_unstraightening Straightening and unstraightening
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            of cartesian fibrations and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            valued in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicategories"} quasicategories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/straightening+functor"} straightening functor
            for more information.
          %h3#relation_to_other_kinds_of_fibrations Relation to other kinds of fibrations
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+fibration"} right fibration
            is a special case of that of Cartesian fibration:
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p The following are equivalent:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to Y
                  is a Cartesian fibration and every edge in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is
                  = succeed "-Cartesian" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  is a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+fibration"} right fibration
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  is a Cartesian fibration and every fiber is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
          .proof
            %h6#proof_8 Proof
            %p
              This is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 2.4.2.4
          %p
            There are also the “categorical fibrations”, the fibrations in the Joyal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_8 Proposition
            %p
              Every Cartesian fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to Y
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              is a fibration with respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Joyal"} Joyal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
          .proof
            %h6#proof_9 Proof
            %p
              This is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 3.3.1.7
          %p
            However, when the base is an
            = succeed "-groupoid," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_over_groupoids
              Proposition (over
              = succeed "-groupoids)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to Y
              be a morphism of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  is a Cartesian fibration
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  is a coCartesian fibration
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joyal+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} categorical fibration
          .proof
            %h6#proof_10 Proof
            %p
              This is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 3.3.1.8
          %p
            There is however another
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure, which does model Cartesian fibrations.
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_9 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi sSet
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet^+/S
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
              of the category of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/marked+simplicial+set"} marked simplicial set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+marked+simplicial+over-sets"} model structure on marked simplicial over-sets
            %p
              An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to S
              is fibrant in that model category precisely if
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the underlying morphism of simplicial sets
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to S
                  is a Cartesian fibration;
              %li
                %p
                  the marked edges in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  are precisely the
                  = succeed "s." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+morphism"} Cartesian morphism
          .proof
            %h6#proof_11 Proof
            %p
              This is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 3.1.4.1
          %h3#adjoints_to_the_inclusion_into_1catc Adjoints to the inclusion into (∞,1)Cat/C
          %p
            The inclusion of the cartesian fibrations and cartesian functors in the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Cat
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi C
                    %mi cart
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi Cat
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)Cat_{/C}^{cart} \subseteq (\infty,1)Cat_{/C}
            has both a left and a right adjoint.
          %p The left adjoint is given by the construction of “free fibrations”
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_10 Proposition
            %p
              For maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to C
              and cartesian fibrations
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q : Y \to C
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Fun
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Fun
                      %mi C
                      %mi cart
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Fun_C(p, q) \simeq Fun_C^{cart}((C \downarrow p), q)
            %p
              Dually, for maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to C
              and cocartesian fibrations
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q : Y \to C
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Fun
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Fun
                      %mi C
                      %mi cocart
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Fun_C(p, q) \simeq Fun_C^{cocart}((p \downarrow C), q)
          .proof
            %h6#proof_12 Proof
            %p
              The cartesian case for mapping spaces is theorem 4.11 of
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#GepnerHaugsengNikolaus15"} Gepner-Haugseng-Nikolaus
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Fun
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Fun
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi q
                      %mi op
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Fun
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                      %mi cart
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi q
                      %mi op
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Fun
                      %mi C
                      %mi cocart
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Fun_C(p,q) \simeq Fun_{C^{op}}(p^{op}, q^{op})^{op}
                    \\simeq \Fun_{C^{op}}^{cart}((C^{op} \downarrow p^{op}), q^{op})^{op}
                    \\simeq \Fun_C^{cocart}((p \downarrow C), q)
          %p On the other side,
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_11 Proposition
            %p
              The inclusions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Cat
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi C
                      %mi cart
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi Cat
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)Cat_{/C}^{cart} \subseteq (\infty,1)Cat_{/C}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Cat
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi C
                      %mi cocart
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi Cat
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)Cat_{/C}^{cocart} \subseteq (\infty,1)Cat_{/C}
              have right adjoints.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_13 Proof
            %p
              We handle the cartesian case. The functor tensor product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - \otimes_C C_{/\bullet}
              is the left adjoint part of an adjunction between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fun
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fun(C^{op}, (\infty,1)Cat)
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)Cat
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \mapsto C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fun
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fun(C^{op}, (\infty,1)Cat)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi Cat
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)Cat_{/C}
            %p
              By the description of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
              as a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} lax (∞,1)-colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fun
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Cat
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi C
                      %mi cart
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fun(C^{op}, (\infty,1)Cat) \to (\infty,1)Cat_{/C}^{cart}
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#projections_from_comma_categories Projections from comma categories
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_12 Proposition
            %p
              Given functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : A \to C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G : B \to C
              between quasi-categories, the projection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F \downarrow G) \to A
              is a Cartesian fibration and the projection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F \downarrow G) \to B
              is a coCartesian fibration.
            %p
              In particular, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a quasi-category, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi eval
                      %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} eval_0 : C^{\Delta^1} \to C
              is a Cartesian fibration and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi eval
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} eval_1 : C^{\Delta^1} \to C
              is a coCartesian fibration.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_14 Proof
            %p Consider the diagram of pullback squares
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi G
                            %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mn 0
                            %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi F
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (F \downarrow G) &amp;\to&amp; (id_C \downarrow G) &amp;\to&amp; B
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow G\!\!
                    \\\
                    (F \downarrow id_C) &amp;\to&amp; C^{\Delta^1} &amp;\xrightarrow{1}&amp; C
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow 0\!\!
                    \\\
                    A &amp;\xrightarrow{F}&amp; C
                    }
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 2.4.7.12
              states the projection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (id_C \downarrow G) \to C
              is a Cartesian fibration. Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F \downarrow G) \to A
              is as well, since fibrations are preserved by pullback. Dually for the other projection.
          %p
            The fiber of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi eval
                    %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} eval_1 : C^{\Delta^1} \to C
            at an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in C
            is the slice category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{/X}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (infinity,1)-Grothendieck construction
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to (\infty,1)Cat : X \mapsto C_{/X}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
            induces the composition map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{/X} \to C_{/Y}
          %h3#cartesian_fibrations_over_one_morphism_and_adjunctions Cartesian fibrations over one morphism and Adjunctions
          %p
            By the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (infinity,1)-Grothendieck construction
            a Cartesian fibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \to \Delta[1]
            corresponds to a morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[1]^{op} \to (\infty,1)Cat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-functor"} (infinity,1)-functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : C \to D
          %p
            Obtaining this through the straightening functor above is tedious, but there is a more immediate way to characterize
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          .un_def
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : K \to \Delta[1]
              a Cartesian fibration with specified equivalences
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    h_0  : C \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} p^{-1}(0)
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi D
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    h_1 : D \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} p^{-1}(1)
            %p
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-functor"} (infinity,1)-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : D \to C
              is
              %strong associated
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              if there exists a commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi K
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    D \times \Delta[1] &amp;&amp;\stackrel{s}{\to}&amp;&amp; K
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \Delta[1]
                    }
            %p such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %mi D
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s|_{D \times \{1\}} = h_1
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %mi D
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s|_{D \times \{0\}} = h_0 \circ f
              %li
                %p
                  for every object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                  we have that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s|_{\{x\} \times \Delta[1]}
                  is a p-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+morphism"} Cartesian morphism
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, def. 5.2.1.1
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : K \to \Delta[1]
            is both a Cartesian fibration as well as a coCartesian fibration, then it determines
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ←
                  %mi D
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C
                  \\stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to}
                  D
                  \\,.
          %p
            Such a pair is a pair of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28infinity%2C1%29-functor"} adjoint (infinity,1)-functor
          %h3#CartOverSimplex Cartesian fibrations over simplices
          %p
            … for the moment see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, section 3.2.2
            …
          %h3#the_universal_cartesian_fibration The universal Cartesian fibration
          %p for the moment see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+fibration+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"}> universal fibration of (∞,1)-categories
              \.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"}> Kan fibration
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anodyne+morphism"} anodyne morphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right%2Fleft+Kan+fibration"}> right/left Kan fibration
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right%2Fleft+anodyne+map"} right/left anodyne map
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+fibration"} inner fibration
            %li
              %p
                %strong> Cartesian fibration
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+fibration+of+dendroidal+sets"} Cartesian fibration of dendroidal sets
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coCartesian+fibration+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operads"} coCartesian fibration of (∞,1)-operads
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/straightening+functor"} straightening functor
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                , section 2.4.2 in
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
            %li#MazelGee15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aaron+Mazel-Gee"}> Aaron Mazel-Gee
                ,
                %em A user’s guide to co/cartesian fibrations
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1510.02402"}> arXiv:1510.02402
                )
            %li#GepnerHaugsengNikolaus15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"}> David Gepner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rune+Haugseng"} Rune Haugseng
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"} Thomas Nikolaus
                %em
                  Lax colimits and free fibrations in
                  = succeed "-categories" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1501.02161"}> arXiv:1501.02161
                )
          %p
            Discussion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+internal+to+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} internal to
            any
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Louis+Martini"}> Louis Martini
              ,
              %em Cocartesian fibrations and straightening internal to an ∞-topos
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.00295"}> arXiv:2204.00295
              \&amp;rbrack;
